{{also|Naff}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Perhaps from {{der|en|pld|-}}, 1960s.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref> Further etymology {{unk|en|nocap=1}}; perhaps a conscious corruption of either {{m|en|fanny}} or {{m|en|eff|eff (off)}} (see {{m|en|naff off}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/næf/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-naff.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|æf|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|Britain|Ireland|Commonwealth|colloquial|Polari}} [[bad|Bad]]; [[tasteless]],  poorly thought out, not workable.
#: {{ux|en|That tie is a bit '''naff''', don’t you think?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robert Llewellyn|title=The Man on Platform Five|year=1998|publisher=Hodder & Stoughton|location=London|page=291|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/manonplatformfiv0000llew_t7q0/page/291/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-340-70789-0|passage=She was an ordinary woman in her dress style; she didn't wear a leather bodice or '''naff''' over-knee plastic spiky-heeled boots.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|role=XXXX|actor=Daniel Craig|year=2004|writer=w:J. J. Connolly|title=Layer Cake|passage=I mean ten years ago a bit of charlie was for pop stars or a celebrities birthday bash. It was demonized by Daily Mail Readers getting drunk in '''naff''' wine bars.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Simon Doonan|en|title=Gay men don't get fat|year=2012|publisher=Blue Rider Press|location=New York|page=206|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/gaymendontgetfat0000doon_w2y3/page/206/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-399-15873-5|passage=Remember, “tacky” means “cheap or glitzy”, whereas “naff” is about stylistic shortcomings which are horrifyingly average and pathetically ordinary. ''The Jersey Shore'' is tacky, but ''The Bachelor'' is '''naff'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/feb/23/amy-winehouse-hologram-tour-cancelled|title=Amy Winehouse could belt out a tune – her naff hologram can’t|author=Barbara Ellen|date=2019-02-24|work=The Guardian|passage= A mere seven years after her tragic death, isn’t it grim and tasteless to send her hologram off on some '''naff''' tour?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=John Naughton|title=A moment’s silence, please, for the death of Mark Zuckerberg’s metaverse|work=The Observer|date=2023-05-13|url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/commentisfree/2023/may/13/death-of-mark-zuckerberg-metaverse-meta-facebook-virtual-reality-ai|issn=0029-7712|passage=Note that last phrase: what actually emerged was a virtual-reality platform called Horizon Worlds, accessible only via '''naff''' and clunky Oculus headsets (think an uncomfortable version of Zoom) {{...|and a virtual wasteland populated by textureless, featureless, legless avatars and landscapes that, as Forbes put it, “look like bad ''Roblox'' levels”.}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Marina Hyde|title=So social media has broken even Elon Musk. I’m forced to ask: U OK hun?|work=The Guardian|date=2025-06-13|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/jun/13/social-media-elon-musk-donald-trump-x-platform|issn=0261-3077|passage=Did you see Elon Musk apologise for some tweets this week? (Please don’t be '''naff''' and call them “X posts”.)}}
# {{lb|en|Polari}} [[heterosexual|Heterosexual]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2004
|author=Pip Granger
|title=Trouble In Paradise
|passage=The omie was a veritable donkey beneath the waistband, darlings.  A donkey!  No wonder your boss-palone is so smitten. I've seen my share, dollies, but this old omiepalone was shaken to the core.  Such a terrible waste on a '''naff''' bloke.
}}

